/** @page grpcrelnotesguide Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    Documentation builds support strict warning checks with \c QORE_GRPC_STRICT_DOCS.
    API links cover the core protobuf and asynchronous I/O modules, and generated
    references preserve cross-module links and three-column protobuf type tables.

    @section grpc_v1_0 grpc Module Version 1.0

    <b>Dependencies</b>: Apache Arrow development libraries and Qore with the built-in
    \c protobuf module and HTTP/2 support. Fedora/RHEL use \c libarrow-devel.
    The module implements the gRPC protocol in Qore and does not require \c libgrpc++.

    <b>Features</b>:
    - initial release
    - dynamic protobuf schema loading (file and string) and serialized descriptor loading
    - protobuf encoding/decoding for all field types
    - protobuf message schema introspection (\c messageSchema(), \c enumValues())
    - file descriptor lookup by symbol and filename (\c serializeFileDescriptorForSymbol(),
      \c serializeFileDescriptorByName())
    - JSON conversion via protobuf
    - gRPC client with unary, server streaming, client streaming, bidirectional streaming
    - gRPC server with handler registration and async I/O
    - TLS/SSL support on client and server
    - custom metadata (request, initial response, trailing)
    - timeout/deadline enforcement
    - connection pooling via HttpClientConnectionManager
    - gRPC status codes and error handling
    - \c GrpcDataProvider module for data provider API integration
    - \c GrpcConnection with \c grpc:// and \c grpcs:// connection schemes
    - \c GrpcDataProviderFactory for factory-based creation
    - \c GrpcTypeHelper for protobuf-to-DataProvider type mapping
    - \c GrpcReflectionClient for gRPC server reflection protocol (client)
    - @ref Grpc::GrpcReflectionService "GrpcReflectionService" for built-in gRPC server
      reflection (\c grpc.reflection.v1) — enables clients to discover services without
      local \c .proto files; also available via the \c enable_reflection
      @ref Qore::Grpc::GrpcServerOptions "GrpcServerOptions" flag
    - <b>Arrow IPC support</b> (optional, requires Apache Arrow):
      - @ref Qore::Grpc::ArrowSchema for schema definition, introspection, and IPC serialization
      - @ref Qore::Grpc::ArrowRecordBatch for columnar data with row/column construction and conversion
      - @ref Qore::Grpc::ArrowIpc static utility class for IPC serialization / deserialization
      - support for all Arrow primitive types, nested types (struct, list, large_list, map),
        decimal128/256, timestamps with timezones, durations, half-float, and field/schema metadata
      - when built with qore Arrow C Data interop, supported \c ColumnarResult
        conversions use libqore's zero-copy Arrow C Data bridge before falling
        back to Arrow builders for types not yet covered by the bridge; builds
        with qore temporal-buffer support keep microsecond timestamp and
        duration columns as dense \c buffer<int64> data while preserving Arrow
        temporal schema
      - IPC data_header + data_body split compatible with Arrow Flight wire format
    - <b>Arrow Flight protocol</b> (optional, requires Apache Arrow):
      - @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightClient "ArrowFlightClient" for Flight RPCs (ListFlights,
        GetFlightInfo, DoGet, DoPut, DoExchange, DoAction)
      - @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightServer "ArrowFlightServer" with dataset and action registration
      - @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightStreamReader "ArrowFlightStreamReader",
        @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightStreamWriter "ArrowFlightStreamWriter", and
        @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightExchangeStream "ArrowFlightExchangeStream" for typed streaming
      - @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightDatasetHandler "ArrowFlightDatasetHandler" abstract base for
        user-implemented Flight datasets
      - @ref Grpc::ArrowFlightHelper "ArrowFlightHelper" for FlightData ↔ Arrow object conversion
      - incoming Flight IPC \c data_header and \c data_body buffers are wrapped without copying
        when decoding record batches
      - @ref Grpc::FlightProto "FlightProto" embedded Flight protocol schema
    - <b>ArrowFlightDataProvider module</b> (optional, requires Apache Arrow):
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightDataProvider "ArrowFlightDataProvider" root
        provider with dataset discovery via ListFlights
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightDatasetDataProvider "ArrowFlightDatasetDataProvider"
        per-dataset container provider
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightMethodDataProvider "ArrowFlightMethodDataProvider"
        method-level provider supporting DoGet, DoPut, and DoExchange
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightStreamEventDataProvider "ArrowFlightStreamEventDataProvider"
        observable event provider for streaming methods
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightConnection "ArrowFlightConnection" with
        \c flight:// and \c flights:// connection schemes
      - @ref ArrowFlightDataProvider::ArrowFlightTypeHelper "ArrowFlightTypeHelper" for
        Arrow-to-DataProvider type mapping
    - <b>SalesforcePubSubDataProvider module</b>: a Salesforce Pub/Sub API event source that
      attaches itself to the Salesforce data provider in the %Qore library as its \c pubsub child,
      so platform events, Change Data Capture events and custom channels drive Qore and Qorus logic
      through the DataProvider observer API
      - @ref SalesforcePubSubDataProvider::SalesforcePubSubEventsDataProvider
        "SalesforcePubSubEventsDataProvider" events container, with one child provider per
        subscribable channel in the org
      - @ref SalesforcePubSubDataProvider::SalesforcePubSubEventDataProvider
        "SalesforcePubSubEventDataProvider" observable provider per channel, with the event type
        derived from the channel's Avro schema
      - @ref SalesforcePubSubDataProvider::SalesforcePubSubClient "SalesforcePubSubClient" for the
        \c eventbus.v1.PubSub service, with the Salesforce call metadata and an Avro schema cache
      - @ref SalesforcePubSubDataProvider::SalesforcePubSubSubscription
        "SalesforcePubSubSubscription" subscription state machine: delivery-driven flow control,
        keepalive handling, replay-ID tracking, token refresh and reconnection with backoff
      - @ref SalesforcePubSubDataProvider::SalesforcePubSubProto "SalesforcePubSubProto", the
        vendored \c pubsub_api.proto as a cached \c ProtobufSchema
*/
